# What the Composer package contains.
#
# Packagist's dist archive is `git archive`, so `export-ignore` is the only
# thing standing between "a PHP project installs a 130KB shim" and "a PHP
# project installs the entire Rust workspace". The published package must hold
# exactly the shim, its metadata, and the notices — nothing else.
#
# The three files that MUST NOT be ignored, and why:
#
#   LICENSE                   Apache-2.0 §4(a): recipients of a derivative or a
#                             distribution get a copy of the licence. The
#                             Composer package is a distribution.
#   THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md   the binary the shim downloads is statically linked
#                             against MIT/BSD/ISC dependencies whose terms
#                             require their notices to accompany it.
#   README.md                 the package's entry point on Packagist.
#
#
# The release workflow's archives are built from a checkout, not from
# `git archive`, so nothing here affects them.

# ── Rust: the whole workspace, its manifests, and its tooling ────────────────
/crates/           export-ignore
/xtask/            export-ignore
/harness/          export-ignore
/spike/            export-ignore
/Cargo.toml        export-ignore
/Cargo.lock        export-ignore
/rustfmt.toml      export-ignore
/clippy.toml       export-ignore
/deny.toml         export-ignore
/about.toml        export-ignore
/about.hbs         export-ignore
/.cargo/           export-ignore

# ── Repository operation: CI, corpus wiring, agent and contributor docs ──────
/.github/          export-ignore
/.claude/          export-ignore
/.gitignore        export-ignore
/.gitattributes    export-ignore
/corpus.lock.toml  export-ignore
/AGENTS.md         export-ignore
/CONTEXT.md        export-ignore

# The changelog is written for someone deciding whether to upgrade, and it is
# already where they would look: `release.yml` uses each version's section
# verbatim as the GitHub Release body. Shipping a second copy into `vendor/`
# adds weight to every install to duplicate the release page.
/CHANGELOG.md      export-ignore

# ── Prose: hundreds of files (ADRs, specs, research) aimed at contributors, ──
# not at someone who installed a linter. The published docs live on the repo.
/docs/             export-ignore

# The shim's own tests. CI runs them from a checkout, never from the published
# archive, so shipping them would only add weight to every `composer install`.
/composer/tests/   export-ignore
